  message: "Phase A audit complete. Lab journal: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_04272026_2159.md.\n\n6-repo measurement (alertmanager + prometheus + kserve + chatwoot + detekt + django, covering Go / Python / Ruby+Vue / Kotlin):\n\n- High-evidence cells (movement on all 6 repos): trivial_sink × {coverage,connectivity,tiered}; utility × same 3; tier × connectivity (only).\n- Medium-evidence cells: noise (django d6-d8 only — Rails migrations triggered the dampener on django but not chatwoot, because django's framework concentrates centrality in shared classes vs. chatwoot's file-per-migration pattern); generated × all 4 surfaces (kserve d14-d42 only — kserve is the only repo with is_generated_file flags); file_kind × {coverage,connectivity} (Go-and-Kotlin-specific d3-d9).\n- Zero-evidence cells: sibling_impl × all 24 surface×repo combinations, including alertmanager (the original WI-luvaj test case). Filing follow-up to investigate why apply_sibling_impl_weights doesn't fire in practice; will still backfill in Phase B for surface uniformity.\n- common_method × all 4 surfaces shows only sporadic d0-d3 movement; not a strong signal but historical bakeoff (WI-luvaj) justifies it.\n\nHistorical investigation confirms WI-lidum's 'residue of organic growth' framing: none of the 8 dampener-introduction commits (2026-01-30 through 2026-04-25) touched sketch.py or compact.py; the one Feb 23 sketch retrofit (fba8673aa0) explicitly identified the same bug class for noopMetric.Inc/Timer.Duration but only fixed 2 of 8 dampeners; compact.py surfaces have never been retrofitted. No ADR documents intentional divergence.\n\nPhase B plan: 3 PRs (sketch first → coverage → connectivity), then a separate PR for the centrality-parameter alignment (now WI-dohaf, bumped P3→P2 based on this audit; see WI-dohaf thread). Each PR tagged awaits_bakeoff_validation at merge."  # 9ba0
